  "@type": "DefinedTerm",
  "alternateName": "Habitat type condition not affected adversely by anthropogenic pressures",
  "description": "The condition of the habitat type, including its biotic and abiotic structure and its\nfunctions (e.g. its typical species composition and their relative abundance, absence\nof particularly sensitive or fragile species\nor species providing a key function, size\nstructure of species), is not adversely affected due to anthropogenic pressures.\nMember States shall establish threshold\nvalues for the condition of each habitat\ntype, ensuring compatibility with related\nvalues set under Descriptors 2, 5 and 8,\nthrough regional or subregional cooperation.",
  "disambiguatingDescription": "This term was created by MBO WP1 task 1.3 with external domain experts during the MARCO-BOLO Project to express that this object is of relevance to the named criterion of the MFSD",
